{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01GNTP9dzT14axemrtxCthHR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D6ZgsTHsynZMD1xWktRWCi","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research PSHA disaggregation notation and Kramer citation","subagent_type":"researcher","prompt":"Research the following specific technical items for a seismic hazard analysis report:\n\n1. In PSHA hazard disaggregation, what is the correct notation convention for the conditional probability of a scenario bin (m_k, r_j, epsilon_l)? Specifically:\n   - Is the standard subscript ordering (magnitude k, distance j, residual l) per Bazzurro and Cornell 1999?\n   - What is the correct normalization condition for conditional probabilities summing to unity?\n   - What is the standard notation for the conditional probability P[M=m_k, R=r_j, epsilon=epsilon_l | I > i*]?\n\n2. Verify the publication year of Steven L. Kramer's textbook \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" - is it 1996 or 1997? Who is the publisher?\n\n3. What is the DOI for Bazzurro and Cornell (1999) \"Disaggregation of seismic hazard\" in the Bulletin of the Seismological Society of America?\n\n4. Is the Borcherdt (2012) reference on Vs30 and site amplification verifiable? What is the correct Borcherdt publication on site classification and Vs30 from around that time period (2010-2015)?\n\nPlease provide authoritative web sources and DOIs for each finding.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4694,"cache_read_input_tokens":80941,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4694,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"a17d036d-f5de-48bc-ae53-8e6279c7ee85"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a7c3d8f2483120646","tool_use_id":"toolu_01D6ZgsTHsynZMD1xWktRWCi","description":"Research PSHA disaggregation notation and Kramer citation","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Research the following specific technical items for a seismic hazard analysis report:\n\n1. In PSHA hazard disaggregation, what is the correct notation convention for the conditional probability of a scenario bin (m_k, r_j, epsilon_l)? Specifically:\n   - Is the standard subscript ordering (magnitude k, distance j, residual l) per Bazzurro and Cornell 1999?\n   - What is the correct normalization condition for conditional probabilities summing to unity?\n   - What is the standard notation for the conditional probability P[M=m_k, R=r_j, epsilon=epsilon_l | I > i*]?\n\n2. Verify the publication year of Steven L. Kramer's textbook \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" - is it 1996 or 1997? Who is the publisher?\n\n3. What is the DOI for Bazzurro and Cornell (1999) \"Disaggregation of seismic hazard\" in the Bulletin of the Seismological Society of America?\n\n4. Is the Borcherdt (2012) reference on Vs30 and site amplification verifiable? What is the correct Borcherdt publication on site classification and Vs30 from around that time period (2010-2015)?\n\nPlease provide authoritative web sources and DOIs for each finding.","uuid":"1f8ebc34-290e-4468-a499-916101d9522d","session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215"}
