{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01GNTP9dzT14axemrtxCthHR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011LJg6Nho39xWPXmYm3mdCS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research TSF seismic design standards AEP values","subagent_type":"researcher","prompt":"Research the following for a technical report on seismic design of tailings storage facilities (TSFs):\n\n1. GISTM (Global Industry Standard on Tailings Management, 2020): What are the exact annual exceedance probability (AEP) criteria for each consequence class (Low, Medium, High, Extreme) during operations and at passive closure? Is the operational range 1/200 (Low) to 1/10,000 (Extreme)? Does passive closure uniformly require 1/10,000 AEP for all classes?\n\n2. CDA (Canadian Dam Association) guidelines 2021 - tailings dam breach analysis technical bulletin: What are the AEP criteria by consequence class (Low to Extreme) during operations? Does the range span 1/100 to 1/10,000? Is there a CDA \"mining dams bulletin\" from 2014 that is distinct from the 2021 technical bulletin?\n\n3. ANCOLD 2019 guidelines on tailings dams: Is the OBE uniformly at approximately 1/500 AEP for all consequence classes during operations? Does the SEE range from 1/1,000 to 1/10,000 by consequence class? Is the 0.1% AEP storm pond criterion (no overtopping during seismic events) confirmed in ANCOLD guidelines?\n\n4. What is the most appropriate edition of NEHRP seismic provisions to cite as current - the 2015 edition (FEMA P-1050) or the 2020 edition (FEMA P-2082)? What changes did the 2020 edition make to site classification?\n\nPlease provide specific URLs and any available DOIs for each finding.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4694,"cache_read_input_tokens":80941,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4694,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"b43742e0-bc98-44bd-b751-ca37c59d6cc0"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a18dd9236086b9aba","tool_use_id":"toolu_011LJg6Nho39xWPXmYm3mdCS","description":"Research TSF seismic design standards AEP values","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Research the following for a technical report on seismic design of tailings storage facilities (TSFs):\n\n1. GISTM (Global Industry Standard on Tailings Management, 2020): What are the exact annual exceedance probability (AEP) criteria for each consequence class (Low, Medium, High, Extreme) during operations and at passive closure? Is the operational range 1/200 (Low) to 1/10,000 (Extreme)? Does passive closure uniformly require 1/10,000 AEP for all classes?\n\n2. CDA (Canadian Dam Association) guidelines 2021 - tailings dam breach analysis technical bulletin: What are the AEP criteria by consequence class (Low to Extreme) during operations? Does the range span 1/100 to 1/10,000? Is there a CDA \"mining dams bulletin\" from 2014 that is distinct from the 2021 technical bulletin?\n\n3. ANCOLD 2019 guidelines on tailings dams: Is the OBE uniformly at approximately 1/500 AEP for all consequence classes during operations? Does the SEE range from 1/1,000 to 1/10,000 by consequence class? Is the 0.1% AEP storm pond criterion (no overtopping during seismic events) confirmed in ANCOLD guidelines?\n\n4. What is the most appropriate edition of NEHRP seismic provisions to cite as current - the 2015 edition (FEMA P-1050) or the 2020 edition (FEMA P-2082)? What changes did the 2020 edition make to site classification?\n\nPlease provide specific URLs and any available DOIs for each finding.","uuid":"e254f77c-7e4c-48e3-8e95-16177536c530","session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215"}
