{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01GNTP9dzT14axemrtxCthHR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WSaGmtAXHfSWoRRgB12Ja2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research Australian and Canadian site classification standards","subagent_type":"researcher","prompt":"Research the following for a seismic hazard technical report:\n\n1. AS 1726-2017 (Australian Standard for geotechnical site investigations): Does it define a site classification system (A through E plus special category S) using shear wave velocity? Does it use a parameter called \"v-bar_S\" for site classification? How does it relate to seismic design?\n\n2. AS 1170.4 (Australian Standard \"Earthquake Actions on Structures\", current edition): Does this standard use the same A-through-E-plus-S site classification? Does it explicitly use shear wave velocity (Vs30) to classify the ground, or does it use a different approach? What are the site classes and their definitions?\n\n3. NBC 2020 (National Building Code of Canada 2020): What are the specific site classification categories (A through F)? What parameters are used (v_s30, SPT blow count, undrained shear strength s_u)? What are the approximate velocity thresholds for each category? Is there any public documentation available?\n\n4. What is the version status of AS 1170.4? Is there a 2007 or later edition? When was the most recent revision?\n\nPlease search for publicly available information from Standards Australia, NRC Canada, and any freely accessible academic or government sources. Provide URLs for any findings.","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4694,"cache_read_input_tokens":80941,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4694,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"6c78fa9d-7830-4a33-8c16-d3df4ea8a35f"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"adc2b39d269ef56be","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WSaGmtAXHfSWoRRgB12Ja2","description":"Research Australian and Canadian site classification standards","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Research the following for a seismic hazard technical report:\n\n1. AS 1726-2017 (Australian Standard for geotechnical site investigations): Does it define a site classification system (A through E plus special category S) using shear wave velocity? Does it use a parameter called \"v-bar_S\" for site classification? How does it relate to seismic design?\n\n2. AS 1170.4 (Australian Standard \"Earthquake Actions on Structures\", current edition): Does this standard use the same A-through-E-plus-S site classification? Does it explicitly use shear wave velocity (Vs30) to classify the ground, or does it use a different approach? What are the site classes and their definitions?\n\n3. NBC 2020 (National Building Code of Canada 2020): What are the specific site classification categories (A through F)? What parameters are used (v_s30, SPT blow count, undrained shear strength s_u)? What are the approximate velocity thresholds for each category? Is there any public documentation available?\n\n4. What is the version status of AS 1170.4? Is there a 2007 or later edition? When was the most recent revision?\n\nPlease search for publicly available information from Standards Australia, NRC Canada, and any freely accessible academic or government sources. Provide URLs for any findings.","uuid":"ddb9109b-c197-4aaa-9af7-e4430371eef7","session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215"}
