{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P6Br8oFtmjJp8Vku2CebGR","type":"tool_result","content":"# Analysis of ASCE7-22 Web Service Documentation\n\nBased on the provided documentation, here's what the page explicitly states about these parameters:\n\n**Formulas Mentioned:**\n\nThe documentation defines the relationships as follows:\n\n1. **SMS formula**: \"SMS = 1.5 x SDS\" - explicitly stated in the response parameters section\n2. **SM1 formula**: \"SM1 = 1.5 x SD1\" - explicitly stated in the response parameters section\n\n**Maximum Direction Conversion Factors:**\n\nThe metadata section includes a \"maxDirectionFactor\" array with ordinates containing the values 1.2, 1.25, 1.3 and others (ranging from 1.2 to 1.3 across different periods).\n\n**VS30 Threshold:**\n\nThe documentation does **not mention** a T* threshold at 442 m/s or 1450 ft/s for SD1 calculation. However, the example response includes \"vs30:530\" in the metadata, indicating VS30 values are tracked, but no specific threshold discussion appears in this documentation.\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe page confirms the first two formulas directly. It includes maximum direction scale factors but provides no explanation of the 442 m/s threshold you referenced."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"3f644b5f-a6b3-43fd-9d3d-aa91af236800","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:30:52.498Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":48872,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Analysis of ASCE7-22 Web Service Documentation\n\nBased on the provided documentation, here's what the page explicitly states about these parameters:\n\n**Formulas Mentioned:**\n\nThe documentation defines the relationships as follows:\n\n1. **SMS formula**: \"SMS = 1.5 x SDS\" - explicitly stated in the response parameters section\n2. **SM1 formula**: \"SM1 = 1.5 x SD1\" - explicitly stated in the response parameters section\n\n**Maximum Direction Conversion Factors:**\n\nThe metadata section includes a \"maxDirectionFactor\" array with ordinates containing the values 1.2, 1.25, 1.3 and others (ranging from 1.2 to 1.3 across different periods).\n\n**VS30 Threshold:**\n\nThe documentation does **not mention** a T* threshold at 442 m/s or 1450 ft/s for SD1 calculation. However, the example response includes \"vs30:530\" in the metadata, indicating VS30 values are tracked, but no specific threshold discussion appears in this documentation.\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe page confirms the first two formulas directly. It includes maximum direction scale factors but provides no explanation of the 442 m/s threshold you referenced.","durationMs":3936,"url":"https://earthquake.usgs.gov/ws/designmaps/asce7-22.html"}}
