{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01KjA7fxnC5PH5a64KZfG18z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The USGS web service confirmed:\n- $S_{MS} = 1.5 \\times S_{DS}$ ✓\n- $S_{M1} = 1.5 \\times S_{D1}$ ✓ (critical correction: the KB has $S_{M1} = 1.5 \\times S_{M1}$ which is wrong)\n- Scale factors 1.2, 1.25, 1.3 are in the maxDirectionFactor array ✓\n\nThe ASCE 7-22 Chapter 21 requires authentication, so I can't verify the log-log interpolation or T* threshold directly.\n\n\nThe GISTM article didn't have the specific AEP values I needed, so I'm looking for other sources that might have them and trying to pin down the publication year for the Kramer textbook.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3531,"cache_read_input_tokens":98245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3531,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"56e66b7d-3475-4821-8e22-14995b8ae10e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01KjA7fxnC5PH5a64KZfG18z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013EVt9ZjLaxVwzQgYZJL2Fy","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://blog.gistm.net/blog/a1-understanding-gistm-complete-overview/","prompt":"What does this page say about Annual Exceedance Probability (AEP) requirements for different consequence classes under GISTM? Look for specific values like 1/200, 1/500, 1/1000, 1/2500, 1/10000. Also look for passive closure requirements and any comparison with other standards. Extract any tables showing AEP values by consequence class and lifecycle phase."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3531,"cache_read_input_tokens":98245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3531,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"19bd5e47-d8fd-4954-9f0f-f4182f375cca"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01KjA7fxnC5PH5a64KZfG18z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HLYNSVuYBNSih5eej4dXQD","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://www.ancold.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Tailings-Guideline-Addendum-July-2019_v2.pdf","prompt":"What does this document say about Operating Basis Earthquake (OBE) and Safety Evaluation Earthquake (SEE) Annual Exceedance Probability (AEP) criteria? Specifically: 1) Is the OBE uniformly at 1/500 AEP for all consequence classes during operations? 2) What is the SEE AEP range by consequence class (1/1000 to 1/10000)? 3) Is there a 0.1% AEP storm pond criterion for concurrent seismic-storm loading? 4) What happens for pre-abandonment - is the MCE or 1/10000 at 85th percentile required?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3531,"cache_read_input_tokens":98245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3531,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"9f452c31-237b-4fb0-a1c8-eb7a8869981f"}
