{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012ohLJ96cctQw43zhJHEk4H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good progress. Let me compile what I've confirmed so far:\n\n1. **$S_{M1} = 1.5 \\times S_{D1}$** is CONFIRMED as the correct formula [WEB:https://earthquake.usgs.gov/ws/designmaps/asce7-22.html]. The source document has $S_{M1} = 1.5 \\times S_{M1}$ which is a critical error.\n\n2. **T* = 2s for v_s > 1,450 ft/s (442 m/s), T* = 5s for v_s ≤ 1,450 ft/s** is CONFIRMED [WEB:https://www.iccsafe.org/building-safety-journal/bsj-technical/is-continued-use-of-the-two-period-design-spectrum-in-the-equivalent-lateral-force-procedure-of-seismic-design-permitted-by-a\n\n3. The scale factors 1.2, 1.25, and 1.3 appear in the USGS API metadata as directional adjustment values, and I'm tracking down the Borcherdt citation since the KB references 2012 but the actual USGS publication appears to be Dobry et al. (2000) with Borcherdt as a co-author.\n\nNow I need to verify the specific Borcherdt 2012 publication, confirm the Kramer textbook edition, locate the GISTM AEP values, and clarify the disaggregation notation being used.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1637,"cache_read_input_tokens":102930,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1637,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"2ba40899-36a2-4da4-ba86-113654afa97b"}
