{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HREzSyYLogBqKH9GXEZVmp","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your question, but I'm unable to extract meaningful information from the provided content. The web page appears to be a PDF document containing compressed/encoded binary data rather than readable text about NEHRP site classification standards.\n\nTo properly answer your questions about:\n- NEHRP velocity thresholds for Site Classes A-F\n- Changes between 2015 and 2020 provisions\n- New sub-classes in FEMA P-2082\n\nI would need access to the actual readable text of the NEHRP standards documents. I'd recommend:\n\n1. Consulting FEMA P-2082 (Seismic Design Reference Manual for the Building Seismic Safety Council)\n2. Reviewing the USGS or ASCE resources on site classification\n3. Accessing the original standards through official FEMA or ASCE publications\n\nIf you can provide the actual text content of these standards, I'd be happy to compare the classification systems and identify any changes or new categories.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 942KB) also saved to /home/averri/.claude/projects/-data-github-tools-tito-examples-review-psha-sessions-run-20260329-222746/e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215/tool-results/webfetch-1774834472774-euev8k.pdf]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"d64bb720-dc9a-42db-be8b-d0426670f3ea","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:34:43.505Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":964602,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"I appreciate your question, but I'm unable to extract meaningful information from the provided content. The web page appears to be a PDF document containing compressed/encoded binary data rather than readable text about NEHRP site classification standards.\n\nTo properly answer your questions about:\n- NEHRP velocity thresholds for Site Classes A-F\n- Changes between 2015 and 2020 provisions\n- New sub-classes in FEMA P-2082\n\nI would need access to the actual readable text of the NEHRP standards documents. I'd recommend:\n\n1. Consulting FEMA P-2082 (Seismic Design Reference Manual for the Building Seismic Safety Council)\n2. Reviewing the USGS or ASCE resources on site classification\n3. Accessing the original standards through official FEMA or ASCE publications\n\nIf you can provide the actual text content of these standards, I'd be happy to compare the classification systems and identify any changes or new categories.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 942KB) also saved to /home/averri/.claude/projects/-data-github-tools-tito-examples-review-psha-sessions-run-20260329-222746/e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215/tool-results/webfetch-1774834472774-euev8k.pdf]","durationMs":10993,"url":"https://www.nehrp.gov/pdf/H-18-8.pdf"}}
