{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01HHzYSaMprEAiUYvjzAmQy9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H1TsZqLpaSY2Wg4YUHqUqA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"S_{M1}=1.5\" /home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_222746/psha_enh1.enhance.md && echo \"---\" && grep -n \"Kramer199\" /home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_222746/psha_enh1.enhance.md && echo \"---\" && grep -n \"theta_{k,j\" /home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_222746/psha_enh1.enhance.md && echo \"---\" && grep -n \"\\\\\\\\text{where}\" /home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_222746/psha_enh1.enhance.md","description":"Verify key corrections in enhanced document"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":147347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":632,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"7b3e2fb2-400f-44f6-9a57-f8887c18d662"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H1TsZqLpaSY2Wg4YUHqUqA","type":"tool_result","content":"40:S_{M1}=1.5\\,S_{D1}\n---\n79:Disaggregation is performed at a target hazard level, defined by an annual exceedance probability or return period. This produces conditional probability distributions over scenario bins and identifies controlling scenario parameters responsible for site hazard [@Kramer1996]. The ground-motion exceedance probability and total annual exceedance rate are defined in the hazard analysis (see [@eq-hazard-integral], [@eq-epsilon-star]). The joint exceedance rate for scenario $(m_k, r_j, \\varepsilon_\\ell)$ from source $s$ is given in [@eq-disagg-rate], where $\\phi$ is the standard normal probability density function and $\\mathbf 1_{{\\cdot}}$ is the indicator function. Integration over $\\varepsilon$ yields the two-dimensional ($M$-$R$) formulation. Partitioning parameter space into magnitude bins $m_k$, distance bins $r_j$, and residual bins $\\varepsilon_\\ell$, the contribution from bin $(k,j,\\ell)$ is in [@eq-disagg-bin].\n80:^[Confidence: MEDIUM, Rationale: The source documents cited this paragraph as [@Kramer1997]; however, the textbook \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" by Steven L. Kramer was published by Prentice-Hall in 1996, not 1997 [WEB:https://www.scirp.org/reference/referencespapers?referenceid=576202][WEB:https://archive.org/details/geotechnicaleart0000kram]. The citation key has been corrected to [@Kramer1996] in this enhanced session output. The Kramer (1996) textbook is an appropriate citation for the concept of conditional probability distributions identifying controlling scenario parameters, as it covers disaggregation methodology at a graduate level. The mathematical framework that follows, using the standard normal PDF $\\phi$ and indicator function $\\mathbf{1}_{(\\cdot)}$ to express the joint exceedance rate, is standard in the disaggregation literature [DOI:10.1785/BSSA0890020501]. Confidence is MEDIUM because the corrected citation year has not been verified against the physical book title page, and the description of the following equations refers to cross-references not reproduced here.]\n---\n102:The conditional probability that exceedance of $i^*$ is produced by bin $(k,j,\\ell)$ is given by [@eq-disagg-prob]. The **modal scenario** is the $(k,j,\\ell)$ bin for which $\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}(i^{*})$ attains its maximum. Hazard disaggregation applies Bayes' theorem to the joint distribution of scenario parameters and ground-motion exceedance as in [@eq-disagg-prob]. The marginal distribution for $\\varepsilon$ quantifies the proportion of exceedance attributable to median or above-median ground-motion residuals. Marginal probabilities are obtained by double summation over the other indices as in [@eq-disagg-marginal-M], [@eq-disagg-marginal-R], [@eq-disagg-marginal-eps]:\n106:P[M=m_k,R=r_j,\\varepsilon=\\varepsilon_\\ell\\mid I> i^{*}] = \\theta_{k,j,\\ell}=\n109:\\sum_{k}\\sum_{j}\\sum_{\\ell}\\theta_{k,j,\\ell} = 1\n113:P\\left[M \\in m_k\\mid I> i^{*}\\right] = \\sum_{j}\\sum_{\\ell}\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}\n116:P\\left[R \\in r_j\\mid I> i^{*}\\right] = \\sum_{k}\\sum_{\\ell}\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}\n119:P\\left[\\varepsilon \\in \\varepsilon_\\ell\\mid I> i^{*}\\right] = \\sum_{k}\\sum_{j}\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}\n---\n30:\\quad \\text{where} \\quad","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"11d531ba-5e5d-4846-8ed7-b7d5d88e3e9c","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:45:59.201Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"40:S_{M1}=1.5\\,S_{D1}\n---\n79:Disaggregation is performed at a target hazard level, defined by an annual exceedance probability or return period. This produces conditional probability distributions over scenario bins and identifies controlling scenario parameters responsible for site hazard [@Kramer1996]. The ground-motion exceedance probability and total annual exceedance rate are defined in the hazard analysis (see [@eq-hazard-integral], [@eq-epsilon-star]). The joint exceedance rate for scenario $(m_k, r_j, \\varepsilon_\\ell)$ from source $s$ is given in [@eq-disagg-rate], where $\\phi$ is the standard normal probability density function and $\\mathbf 1_{{\\cdot}}$ is the indicator function. Integration over $\\varepsilon$ yields the two-dimensional ($M$-$R$) formulation. Partitioning parameter space into magnitude bins $m_k$, distance bins $r_j$, and residual bins $\\varepsilon_\\ell$, the contribution from bin $(k,j,\\ell)$ is in [@eq-disagg-bin].\n80:^[Confidence: MEDIUM, Rationale: The source documents cited this paragraph as [@Kramer1997]; however, the textbook \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" by Steven L. Kramer was published by Prentice-Hall in 1996, not 1997 [WEB:https://www.scirp.org/reference/referencespapers?referenceid=576202][WEB:https://archive.org/details/geotechnicaleart0000kram]. The citation key has been corrected to [@Kramer1996] in this enhanced session output. The Kramer (1996) textbook is an appropriate citation for the concept of conditional probability distributions identifying controlling scenario parameters, as it covers disaggregation methodology at a graduate level. The mathematical framework that follows, using the standard normal PDF $\\phi$ and indicator function $\\mathbf{1}_{(\\cdot)}$ to express the joint exceedance rate, is standard in the disaggregation literature [DOI:10.1785/BSSA0890020501]. Confidence is MEDIUM because the corrected citation year has not been verified against the physical book title page, and the description of the following equations refers to cross-references not reproduced here.]\n---\n102:The conditional probability that exceedance of $i^*$ is produced by bin $(k,j,\\ell)$ is given by [@eq-disagg-prob]. The **modal scenario** is the $(k,j,\\ell)$ bin for which $\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}(i^{*})$ attains its maximum. Hazard disaggregation applies Bayes' theorem to the joint distribution of scenario parameters and ground-motion exceedance as in [@eq-disagg-prob]. The marginal distribution for $\\varepsilon$ quantifies the proportion of exceedance attributable to median or above-median ground-motion residuals. Marginal probabilities are obtained by double summation over the other indices as in [@eq-disagg-marginal-M], [@eq-disagg-marginal-R], [@eq-disagg-marginal-eps]:\n106:P[M=m_k,R=r_j,\\varepsilon=\\varepsilon_\\ell\\mid I> i^{*}] = \\theta_{k,j,\\ell}=\n109:\\sum_{k}\\sum_{j}\\sum_{\\ell}\\theta_{k,j,\\ell} = 1\n113:P\\left[M \\in m_k\\mid I> i^{*}\\right] = \\sum_{j}\\sum_{\\ell}\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}\n116:P\\left[R \\in r_j\\mid I> i^{*}\\right] = \\sum_{k}\\sum_{\\ell}\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}\n119:P\\left[\\varepsilon \\in \\varepsilon_\\ell\\mid I> i^{*}\\right] = \\sum_{k}\\sum_{j}\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}\n---\n30:\\quad \\text{where} \\quad","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
