{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sfjx17uVR2xchAfp2bhWTa","type":"tool_result","content":"6:Chapter §11.4.7 indicates that to perform a site response analysis and a ground motion hazard analysis to determine ground motions for any structure, procedures of sections §21.1 and §21.2 must be applied.\n7:^[Confidence: MEDIUM, Rationale: The substance of this statement -- that §11.4.7 requires compliance with §21.1 and §21.2 for site-specific hazard analysis -- is consistent with the hierarchical structure of ASCE 7-22 as described in publicly available documentation [WEB:https://earthquake.usgs.gov/ws/designmaps/asce7-22.html]. The grammatical error present in the source document (\"indicate\" instead of \"indicates\") has been corrected in this paragraph. Confidence is MEDIUM rather than HIGH because exact normative clause wording requires access to the licensed standard document.]\n192:^[Confidence: HIGH, Rationale: The envelope approach for defining the design spectral ordinate as the maximum of the GMPE-based and amplification-based estimates across all return periods, oscillator periods, and $V_{S30}$ values is a technically sound and conservative methodology consistent with standard engineering practice for site-specific PSHA [WEB:https://peer.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/webpeer-2014-16-jonathan_p._stewart_kioumars_afshari_and_youssef_m.a._hashash.pdf]. The reference to fractile $p$ indicates awareness of the probabilistic nature of the amplification factor, which is appropriate.]\n---\n93:\\lambda_{k,j,\\ell}(i^{*})=\n107:\\frac{\\lambda_{k,j,\\ell}(i^{*})}{\\lambda_{I}(i^{*})},","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"8623c7c7-2e98-43e0-9631-aec8230e5bdd","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:46:07.624Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"6:Chapter §11.4.7 indicates that to perform a site response analysis and a ground motion hazard analysis to determine ground motions for any structure, procedures of sections §21.1 and §21.2 must be applied.\n7:^[Confidence: MEDIUM, Rationale: The substance of this statement -- that §11.4.7 requires compliance with §21.1 and §21.2 for site-specific hazard analysis -- is consistent with the hierarchical structure of ASCE 7-22 as described in publicly available documentation [WEB:https://earthquake.usgs.gov/ws/designmaps/asce7-22.html]. The grammatical error present in the source document (\"indicate\" instead of \"indicates\") has been corrected in this paragraph. Confidence is MEDIUM rather than HIGH because exact normative clause wording requires access to the licensed standard document.]\n192:^[Confidence: HIGH, Rationale: The envelope approach for defining the design spectral ordinate as the maximum of the GMPE-based and amplification-based estimates across all return periods, oscillator periods, and $V_{S30}$ values is a technically sound and conservative methodology consistent with standard engineering practice for site-specific PSHA [WEB:https://peer.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/webpeer-2014-16-jonathan_p._stewart_kioumars_afshari_and_youssef_m.a._hashash.pdf]. The reference to fractile $p$ indicates awareness of the probabilistic nature of the amplification factor, which is appropriate.]\n---\n93:\\lambda_{k,j,\\ell}(i^{*})=\n107:\\frac{\\lambda_{k,j,\\ell}(i^{*})}{\\lambda_{I}(i^{*})},","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
