{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\nThe session was initiated as a Hive Mind Queen coordinator task. The objective was to run an \"enhance\" session on two prior audited seismic hazard review sessions. Specifically:\n- Read the workflow, format rules, citation rules, and audit rules from `/usr/local/libexec/tito/`\n- Read two source review sessions (psha_hive.review.md and psha_hive2.review.md)\n- Identify LOW and MEDIUM confidence gaps in those sessions\n- Research the gaps using web sources to gather authoritative external evidence\n- Produce a fully audited enhanced manuscript with per-paragraph `^[Confidence: ..., Rationale: ...]` footnotes\n- Write the output to: `/home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_222746/psha_enh1.enhance.md`\n- Output filename was confirmed from the manifest.json file (`outputs.primary: \"psha_enh1.enhance.md\"`)\n- The task.enhance.md said: improve seismic hazard study sections, resolving LOW/MEDIUM findings, strengthening claims, correcting errors. Output must be in ENGLISH.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n- **Enhance Session Workflow**: Gap-focused research over audited sessions; corrects LOW/MEDIUM confidence paragraphs using external web sources; all citations in TOKEN form [WEB:...], [DOI:...], [ARXIV:...], [KB:...]; per-paragraph audit footnotes mandatory\n- **Audit Footnotes**: Format `^[Confidence: HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW, Rationale: ...]` after every prose paragraph; code blocks and display math are not paragraphs and do not get footnotes\n- **Citation Policy**: Enhance sessions use TOKEN citations ([WEB:...], [DOI:...]) not [@Key] for new material; existing [@Key] in body text preserved for compile-enhance step\n- **ASCE 7-22 §21**: Site-specific ground motion procedures; §11.4.7 permits replacement of mapped spectral values; §21.1 (probabilistic), §21.2 (deterministic), §21.3 (design spectrum = 2/3 × MCER), §21.4 (S_DS, S_D1 formulas)\n- **MCER parameters**: S_MS = 1.5 × S_DS; S_M1 = 1.5 × S_D1 (these are the back-calculations from design-level to MCER-level)\n- **RotD50 to RotD100 scale factors**: 1.2 at T ≤ 0.2 s, 1.25 at T = 1.0 s, 1.3 at T ≥ 10 s per ASCE 7-22 §21.1; standard says \"linear interpolation\" between anchors but practitioners apply in log-period space\n- **T* velocity threshold**: 442 m/s (1450 ft/s) in S_D1 formula; T*=2s for v̄_s > 442 m/s, T*=5s for v̄_s ≤ 442 m/s\n- **PSHA Disaggregation**: Bazzurro & Cornell (1999), DOI:10.1785/BSSA0890020501; standard subscript ordering is (k=magnitude, j=distance, ℓ=epsilon)\n- **TSF Seismic Design Standards**: GISTM (2020), CDA (2021 breach analysis bulletin + 2014 mining dams bulletin), ANCOLD (2019); consequence-class-based AEPs; ANCOLD OBE ~1/500 AEP uniform, SEE 1/1,000–1/10,000 by class\n- **NEHRP Site Classification**: 2020 edition (FEMA P-2082) expanded from 6 classes (A-F) to 9 classes (A, B, BC, C, CD, D, DE, E, F); now Vs30-only basis; 2015 edition (FEMA P-1050) = BSSC2015\n- **Vs30**: Harmonic-mean shear-wave velocity over upper 30 m; primary site parameter in NGA-West2 and NGA-East GMPEs\n- **Site Effects**: Two-model approach (ergodic GMPE logic tree + nonlinear amplification model based on Stewart/Hashash 2020); envelope of both governs design\n- **Kramer textbook**: \"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\" by Steven L. Kramer, Prentice-Hall, 1996 (NOT 1997 as cited in source documents)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n- **`/usr/local/libexec/tito/workflows/enhance.session.md`** - Workflow instructions: read MANIFEST for output filename, read source sessions, identify LOW/MEDIUM gaps, research with web, draft corrected paragraphs with TOKEN citations, apply per-paragraph audit, write to SESSION_DIR/outputs.primary\n\n- **`/usr/local/libexec/tito/rules/format.session.md`** - Format rules: professional/academic voice; LaTeX math ($...$ inline, $...$ display); ASCII-only text; no em-dashes (use hyphen); no promotional language; de-duplication\n\n- **`/usr/local/libexec/tito/rules/citations.enhance.md`** - TOKEN citations only in enhance sessions: [KB:...], [WEB:...], [DOI:...], [ARXIV:...]; do not convert to [@Key]; external citations required for all new claims\n\n- **`/usr/local/libexec/tito/rules/audit.md`** - Audit rules: `^[Confidence: HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW, Rationale: ...]` after every paragraph; code blocks and display math blocks are NOT paragraphs; no pass-through\n\n- **`/home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_222746/manifest.json`**\n  - Confirms output filename: `psha_enh1.enhance.md`\n  - Content: `{\"id\": \"psha_enh1\", \"workflow\": \"enhance\", \"inputs\": {\"sources\": [...]}, \"outputs\": {\"primary\": \"psha_enh1.enhance.md\"}}`\n\n- **`/home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/tasks/task.enhance.md`**\n  - \"Improve the seismic hazard study sections by: Resolving any LOW or MEDIUM confidence findings from the review / Strengthening claims with additional authoritative references where needed / Correcting any identified errors or inconsistencies / The output must be in ENGLISH.\"\n\n- **`/home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_195849/psha_hive.review.md`** (251 lines) - First source review session; covers MCER, TSF criteria, disaggregation, PSHA, site effects, site classification with per-paragraph audit footnotes\n\n- **`/home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_214042/psha_hive2.review.md`** (224 lines) - Second source review session; same sections with different/additional DOI citations in some footnotes\n\n- **KB files** (`criteria_MCER.qmd`, `criteria_TSF.qmd`, `disaggregation.qmd`, `hazard.qmd`, `site.qmd`, `site_class.qmd`) - Original knowledge base source files; provided context for what the source documents were reviewing\n\n- **`/home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_222746/psha_enh1.enhance.md`** (257 lines) - **THE OUTPUT FILE** - Created and then edited three times. Full enhanced manuscript with all corrections applied. Structure:\n\n```\n## MCER and ELastic Design Spectra (ASCE) {#sec-mcer}\n[Para 1 - ASCE 7-22 adoption - HIGH]\n[Para 2 - §11.4.7 indicates (grammar fix) - MEDIUM]\n[Para 3 - §21.3/§21.4 chain - HIGH]\n[Para 4 - Probabilistic accelerations/scale factors - MEDIUM]\n[Para 5 - 2/3 factor - HIGH]\n$ S_a = (2/3) S_aM $\n[Para 6 - S_DS/S_D1 formulas with \"where\" fix - MEDIUM]\n$ S_DS formula $ $ S_D1 formula with T* where v_s>442 m/s $\n[Para 7 - S_MS/S_M1 with CRITICAL CORRECTION - HIGH]\n$ S_MS = 1.5 S_DS, S_M1 = 1.5 S_D1 $   ← CORRECTED from S_M1=1.5 S_M1\n\n[TSF frameworks - HIGH]\n[Lifecycle phases - MEDIUM]\n[Framework comparison - MEDIUM]\n### Construction [restored CDA 2014 citation - MEDIUM]\n### Operation (Active Life) [removed unverifiable 0.1% AEP - MEDIUM]\n### Closure and Post-Closure [MEDIUM]\n[Closure engineering principles - MEDIUM]\n\n---YAML separator---\n\n[Disaggregation intro - HIGH]\n[Disaggregation procedure with Kramer1996 fix - MEDIUM]\n$ eq-disagg-rate $\n$ eq-disagg-bin $\n[Modal scenario para with corrected notation - MEDIUM]\n$ eq-disagg-prob CORRECTED: theta_{k,j,ell}, sum theta=1 $\n$ eq-disagg-marginal-M: sum_{j}sum_{ell} theta_{k,j,ell} $\n$ eq-disagg-marginal-R: sum_{k}sum_{ell} theta_{k,j,ell} $\n$ eq-disagg-marginal-eps: sum_{k}sum_{j} theta_{k,j,ell} $\n[Concluding para - HIGH]\n\n[PSHA intro - HIGH]\n$ eq-hazard-integral $\n[Multi-source para - HIGH]\n$ eq-hazard-sum $\n[GMPE sigma para - HIGH]\n[AEP para - HIGH]\n$ eq-aep $\n[Return period para - HIGH]\n\n---YAML separator---\n\n[Site effects intro - HIGH]\n[GMPE-based model - MEDIUM]\n[Amplification model - HIGH]\n$ eq-site-lnf $\n[Mean decomposition - HIGH]\n$ eq-site-sigma-decomp $\n[Dispersion components - HIGH]\n$ eq-site-af $\n[Envelope intro - HIGH]\n$ eq-site-envelope $\n[Envelope rationale - HIGH]\n\n## Site Classification\n[Vs30 intro - HIGH]\n$ V_S30 formula $\n[Formula explanation - HIGH]\n[Vs30 in GMPEs/Borcherdt - MEDIUM]\n[1D site response - HIGH]\n### NEHRP Site Classes\n[9-class system intro para - HIGH] ← MAJOR UPDATE: 6→9 classes\n[9-class bullet list with BC, CD, DE - MEDIUM]\n[Class F explanation - HIGH]\n### AS1726 Guidelines [MEDIUM]\n### ASCE/SEI 7-22 Guidelines [HIGH]\n### NBC-2020 Guidelines [MEDIUM]\n```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n- **Critical equation error** ($S_{M1} = 1.5\\,S_{M1}$ circular tautology in source KB): Corrected to $S_{M1} = 1.5\\,S_{D1}$; confirmed by USGS ASCE 7-22 web service; paragraph confidence upgraded from LOW to HIGH\n- **Grammar error** (\"Chapter §11.4.7 indicate\"): Corrected to \"indicates\"; remains MEDIUM confidence because paraphrase of licensed text\n- **Language/localization error** (`\\text{con}` in equation, Spanish for \"with\"): Corrected to `\\text{where}`; confirmed this is Spanish mathematical notation convention\n- **Citation year error** ([@Kramer1997]): Corrected to [@Kramer1996]; confirmed Prentice-Hall 1996 by multiple sources (Scribd, SCIRP, Archive.org)\n- **Disaggregation notation errors**: Three errors corrected: (1) $\\theta_{j,k,l}$ → $\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}$ (subscript ordering magnitude-first, proper LaTeX ell); (2) $\\lambda_{k,j\\ell}$ → $\\lambda_{k,j,\\ell}$ (missing comma); (3) malformed normalization $\\sum P_{k,j,\\ell}([I>i^*]=1$ → $\\sum\\theta_{k,j,\\ell} = 1$ (correct Bayesian normalization)\n- **Incorrectly removed CDA 2014 citation**: Initially removed as \"unverifiable\" - CORRECTED when research agent a18dd9236086b9aba confirmed the CDA Technical Bulletin: Application of Dam Safety Guidelines to Mining Dams (2014) IS a real and distinct publication from the 2021 breach analysis bulletin\n- **Interpolation description**: Initially wrote \"log-log interpolation\" - corrected to \"linear interpolation applied in log-period space\" after research agent a577f1b18e59533e7 clarified that ASCE 7-22 §21.1 specifies \"linear interpolation\" (practitioners then apply on log-period axis)\n- **NEHRP citation scope**: Initially described only \"BC and CD\" sub-classes - expanded to full 9-class system (A, B, BC, C, CD, D, DE, E, F) after research agent confirmed the complete expansion from FEMA P-2082\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n- **Large file reads**: Source files exceeded 10,000 token limit; solved by reading in chunks of ~80 lines at a time\n- **Paywalled standards**: ASCE 7-22 full text, GISTM full text, CDA bulletins, ANCOLD 2019, AS1726, NBC 2020 all paywalled or binary PDF; addressed by using USGS API documentation, ICC articles, NIST announcements, and multiple secondary sources as external evidence\n- **Unresolvable gaps**: Several MEDIUM confidence items could not be elevated to HIGH due to paywalled primary sources (specific GISTM AEP tables, CDA specific per-class AEPs, AS1726/AS1170.4 classification details, NBC 2020 details); these retained MEDIUM confidence with explanatory rationale\n- **Concurrent research**: 4 background agents launched in parallel; 2 returned during session (a577f1b18e59533e7 and a18dd9236086b9aba); their findings were incorporated into the final document via edits\n\n6. All user messages:\n- Initial Hive Mind system prompt: Full task specification with MANIFEST, TASK, OUTPUT, KB, SOURCES, WORKFLOW, FORMAT_RULES, CITATIONS_RULES, AUDIT_RULES paths; 4 workers; hierarchical-mesh topology; byzantine consensus; instructions to read workflow/rules, identify LOW/MEDIUM gaps, research, produce enhanced manuscript\n- Background agent completion notification for agent a18dd9236086b9aba (TSF seismic design standards AEP values) - confirmed CDA 2014 bulletin exists, NEHRP 9-class expansion details\n- Background agent completion notification for agent a577f1b18e59533e7 (ASCE 7-22 MCER scale factors) - confirmed all 5 verification items, clarified interpolation is \"linear\" per code text applied in log-period space\n- Final message: Request for plain-text summary (no tools) covering the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n- Two background research agents have not yet returned results:\n  - Agent a7c3d8f2483120646: \"Research PSHA disaggregation notation and Kramer citation\" - would have confirmed or added to the notation corrections\n  - Agent adc2b39d269ef56be: \"Research Australian and Canadian site classification standards\" - would have addressed AS1726-2017, AS1170.4, NBC 2020 MEDIUM confidence gaps\n- Their results could potentially upgrade the AS1726/AS1170.4 and NBC 2020 paragraphs from MEDIUM confidence if they found additional public-domain information\n- However, the main output file has been written and the task is substantively complete\n\n8. Current Work:\nThe most recent work was the final edit to the enhanced document to correct the interpolation description. The edit changed:\n\nFrom: `\"log-log interpolation is applied between these period-anchored values\"`\n\nTo: `\"linear interpolation between these period-anchored values is specified in §21.1, and is applied in log-period space consistent with standard spectral analysis convention\"`\n\nAnd updated the audit footnote rationale to: `\"The scale factors 1.2, 1.25, and 1.3 at period breakpoints 0.2 s, 1.0 s, and 10 s are confirmed in the USGS ASCE 7-22 web service metadata; they are based on empirical RotD100/RotD50 ratios from Shahi and Baker (2014). The standard text specifies linear interpolation between anchored values; practitioners and the USGS API apply this in log-period space.\"`\n\nThe final output file `/home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_222746/psha_enh1.enhance.md` was confirmed created at 257 lines. All corrections verified via grep:\n- Line 40: `S_{M1}=1.5\\,S_{D1}` (corrected)\n- Line 79: `[@Kramer1996]` (corrected)\n- Lines 106, 109, 113, 116, 119: `\\theta_{k,j,\\ell}` (corrected throughout)\n- Line 30: `\\text{where}` (corrected)\n- Line 6: \"indicates\" (corrected)\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\nThe primary task is complete - the enhanced session document has been written to the specified output path. The workflow concludes with: \"Confirm in your final message (without printing document contents): 'Enhanced session document written to {{SESSION_DIR}}/psha_enh1.enhance.md'\"\n\nThe task was concluded with the message:\n> \"Enhanced session document written to `/home/averri/github/tools/tito-examples/review/psha/sessions/run-20260329_222746/psha_enh1.enhance.md`\"\n\nNo further steps are required unless the two pending background agents (a7c3d8f2483120646 on disaggregation notation, adc2b39d269ef56be on Australian/Canadian standards) return results that suggest additional corrections - but since the session is being summarized/concluded, their results would need to be incorporated in a subsequent session if deemed necessary.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/averri/.claude/projects/-data-github-tools-tito-examples-review-psha-sessions-run-20260329-222746/e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0bf7093-818d-4370-9615-a0aeec356215","uuid":"6c1338ef-6d0f-4b8a-ae39-40398bb21852","timestamp":"2026-03-30T01:50:57.123Z","isSynthetic":true}
